# --- Real dataset and generated data (tens of GB -- never tracked) ---
Flug_100/
Flug_100.zip

# --- Blender visualization project (multi-GB .blend files + rendered videos) ---
blender_vis/

# --- Presentation (binary office doc, not core to the code repo) ---
Urban_Radiance_Field.pptx

# --- DJI's proprietary Thermal SDK DLLs (redistributed binaries, not our code) ---
dji_thermal_sdk_dlls/
dji_thermal_sdk_v*.zip

# --- Editor / tool local state ---
.claude/settings.local.json
.vscode/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- OS junk ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Local environment ---
.env

DJI_H30T_SampleData

# --- White paper / write-up (drafted outside the repo; kept local) ---
# The figures stay tracked in docs/figures/, and so does scripts/make_paper_figures.py,
# which only renders the scene maps. Hidden here: the report itself and the graphical
# abstract that exists only for it.
scripts/make_graphical_abstract.py
docs/whitepaper/
docs/report/
docs/*whitepaper*
docs/*white_paper*
docs/*report*

# --- Handover bundle for a collaborator (4 GB of copied data; built on demand) ---
handover/

# --- Web viewer's generated assets (~26 MB, rebuilt in under 4 minutes) ---
# The viewer's own source in web/ IS tracked; only the binaries the two scripts derive from
# the flight are not, for the same reason Flug_100/ is not: they are outputs, and re-running
# them writes new bytes every time, which would grow the history on each rebuild.
#
#   python scripts/precompute_attribution.py && python scripts/make_web_assets.py
#
# To deploy to GitHub Pages or any other static host, either build them in CI with those two
# commands, or `git add -f web/data/` once and let them ride along -- 26 MB is well inside
# what a repo carries comfortably, it just should not be the silent default.
web/data/
